*> A tensor-product B-spline surface fit: z ~ bs(x, y) on an 8x8 grid.
*> CMD: just TARGET=bspline_ex run-cobol
IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
PROGRAM-ID. BSPLINE-EX.
DATA DIVISION.
WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
COPY "datamunge.cpy".

*> The grid: 64 samples of z = sin(x) + y^2 over [0, 1]^2.
01 GRID.
   05 GRID-X USAGE COMP-2 OCCURS 64.
   05 GRID-Y USAGE COMP-2 OCCURS 64.
   05 GRID-Z USAGE COMP-2 OCCURS 64.
01 IX        USAGE BINARY-LONG.
01 IY        USAGE BINARY-LONG.
01 I         USAGE BINARY-LONG.

01 DATA-FRAME USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
01 NEW-POINTS USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
01 SURFACE   USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
01 PRED      USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
01 PRED-1    PIC -9.9(6).
01 PRED-2    PIC -9.9(6).

PROCEDURE DIVISION.
    MOVE 0 TO I
    PERFORM VARYING IY FROM 0 BY 1 UNTIL IY > 7
        PERFORM VARYING IX FROM 0 BY 1 UNTIL IX > 7
            ADD 1 TO I
            COMPUTE GRID-X(I) = IX / 7.0
            COMPUTE GRID-Y(I) = IY / 7.0
            COMPUTE GRID-Z(I) = FUNCTION SIN(GRID-X(I)) + GRID-Y(I) * GRID-Y(I)
        END-PERFORM
    END-PERFORM

    CALL "dm_data_frame_new" USING DM-DATA-FRAME-NEW DM-STATUS
    PERFORM CHECK
    MOVE DM-DATA-FRAME-NEW-RESULT TO DATA-FRAME
    MOVE DATA-FRAME TO DM-DATA-FRAME-ADD-NUMERIC-COLUMN-SELF
    MOVE 64 TO DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-TABLE-COUNT
    PERFORM VARYING I FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL I > 64
        MOVE GRID-X(I) TO DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-TABLE-ITEM(I)
    END-PERFORM
    MOVE "x" TO DM-DATA-FRAME-ADD-NUMERIC-COLUMN-COLUMN-NAME
    PERFORM ADD-COLUMN
    PERFORM VARYING I FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL I > 64
        MOVE GRID-Y(I) TO DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-TABLE-ITEM(I)
    END-PERFORM
    MOVE "y" TO DM-DATA-FRAME-ADD-NUMERIC-COLUMN-COLUMN-NAME
    PERFORM ADD-COLUMN
    PERFORM VARYING I FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL I > 64
        MOVE GRID-Z(I) TO DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-TABLE-ITEM(I)
    END-PERFORM
    MOVE "z" TO DM-DATA-FRAME-ADD-NUMERIC-COLUMN-COLUMN-NAME
    PERFORM ADD-COLUMN

    MOVE DATA-FRAME TO DM-LM-NEW-DATA
    MOVE "z ~ bs(x, y)" TO DM-LM-NEW-FORMULA
    CALL "dm_lm_new" USING DM-LM-NEW DM-STATUS
    PERFORM CHECK
    MOVE DM-LM-NEW-RESULT TO SURFACE
    DISPLAY "Fitted z ~ bs(x, y)"
    MOVE SURFACE TO DM-LM-PRINT-SUMMARY-SELF
    CALL "dm_lm_print_summary" USING DM-LM-PRINT-SUMMARY DM-STATUS
    PERFORM CHECK

    *> Two new points to predict.
    CALL "dm_data_frame_new" USING DM-DATA-FRAME-NEW DM-STATUS
    PERFORM CHECK
    MOVE DM-DATA-FRAME-NEW-RESULT TO NEW-POINTS
    MOVE NEW-POINTS TO DM-DATA-FRAME-ADD-NUMERIC-COLUMN-SELF
    MOVE 2 TO DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-TABLE-COUNT
    MOVE 0.25 TO DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-TABLE-ITEM(1)
    MOVE 0.75 TO DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-TABLE-ITEM(2)
    MOVE "x" TO DM-DATA-FRAME-ADD-NUMERIC-COLUMN-COLUMN-NAME
    PERFORM ADD-COLUMN
    MOVE 0.50 TO DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-TABLE-ITEM(1)
    MOVE 0.25 TO DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-TABLE-ITEM(2)
    MOVE "y" TO DM-DATA-FRAME-ADD-NUMERIC-COLUMN-COLUMN-NAME
    PERFORM ADD-COLUMN

    MOVE SURFACE TO DM-LM-PREDICT-SELF
    MOVE NEW-POINTS TO DM-LM-PREDICT-NEWDATA
    CALL "dm_lm_predict" USING DM-LM-PREDICT DM-STATUS
    PERFORM CHECK
    MOVE DM-LM-PREDICT-RESULT TO PRED
    MOVE PRED TO DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-TABLE-SELF
    CALL "dm_vector_double_to_table" USING DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-TABLE DM-STATUS
    PERFORM CHECK
    MOVE DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-TABLE-ITEM(1) TO PRED-1
    MOVE DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-TABLE-ITEM(2) TO PRED-2
    DISPLAY "Predictions: [" FUNCTION TRIM(PRED-1) ", " FUNCTION TRIM(PRED-2) "]"

    MOVE PRED TO DM-HANDLE-SELF
    CALL "dm_close" USING DM-HANDLE DM-STATUS
    MOVE SURFACE TO DM-HANDLE-SELF
    CALL "dm_close" USING DM-HANDLE DM-STATUS
    MOVE NEW-POINTS TO DM-HANDLE-SELF
    CALL "dm_close" USING DM-HANDLE DM-STATUS
    MOVE DATA-FRAME TO DM-HANDLE-SELF
    CALL "dm_close" USING DM-HANDLE DM-STATUS
    STOP RUN.

*> Adds the VECTOR-DOUBLE-TABLE items as a column of DM-DATA-FRAME-ADD-NUMERIC-COLUMN-SELF.
ADD-COLUMN.
    CALL "dm_vector_double_from_table" USING DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-TABLE DM-STATUS
    PERFORM CHECK
    MOVE DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-TABLE-SELF TO DM-DATA-FRAME-ADD-NUMERIC-COLUMN-VALUES
    CALL "dm_data_frame_add_numeric_column" USING DM-DATA-FRAME-ADD-NUMERIC-COLUMN DM-STATUS
    PERFORM CHECK
    MOVE DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-TABLE-SELF TO DM-HANDLE-SELF
    CALL "dm_close" USING DM-HANDLE DM-STATUS.

*> Stops with the error after a failed call.
CHECK.
    IF NOT DM-STATUS-OK
        DISPLAY "datamunge error (" FUNCTION TRIM(DM-STATUS-KIND) "): "
            DM-STATUS-MESSAGE(1:DM-STATUS-LENGTH) UPON SYSERR
        STOP RUN RETURNING 1
    END-IF.
